From 39397a8a82295154826e6a12afaa61c8ba513c90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Advait Johari <zakethegr8@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:04:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Restart only changed stations on the Vivid-Hosting AP

A "wifi reload" on the VH-113's Qualcomm firmware deletes and recreates every interface on the radio,
so configuring one station kicks every robot off. When the channel, bandwidth and VLANs are
unchanged, restart hostapd on only the interfaces whose SSID or WPA key changes, through hostapd's
global control socket the way QSDK's hostapd.sh does. Anything else, or a station that doesn't come
back with its new SSID, falls back to reloading all of Wi-Fi as before.
